    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0493" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg481"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 PW/5–1745</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sansom</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Chief of the Division of Japanese Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dickover</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-17">May 17, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Dick</hi>: With reference to our conversation
                    in which you informed me of some statements made in Tokyo to the Swedish
                    Minister by certain Japanese individuals, I send you herewith the substance of a
                    telegram just received from the Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>You will see that the Foreign Office, like the Department of State, did not
                    regard the statements quoted as amounting to a peace feeler; and that some
                    additional information as to remarks made by Prince Konoye<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d350-f1"/> is included in their message.</p>
                <p>We have just received your memorandum of May 14th<anchor n="6" xml:id="d350-f2"/>
                    regarding <pb facs="0494" n="482" xml:id="pg482"/> the views of the Japanese
                    Counsellor at Lisbon, and have transmitted it to the Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d350-a1.xml" xpointer="d350-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d350-f1" n="5" xml:id="d350-f1-content">
                <p>Prince Fumimaro Konoye, Japanese Prime Minister, June 1937–January 1939, and July
                    22, 1940–October 16, 1941.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d350-f2" n="6" xml:id="d350-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 97, <ref target="#pg478">p. 478</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
